{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Negev.</b> The south side, and so it is called in Aramaic, 'נגיבו מיא,' for they are the south side, and from the abundance of heat it dries up. So too the meaning of 'for the land of the Negev you have given me' (Joshua 15:19)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrase 'נגיבו מיא' is apparently cited from Targum Jonathan to Judges 1:15 (the parallel to the Joshua verse); its exact source is not specified in the commentary."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:22.462246835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}